l input files (VCFs, VEPs, populations, configs) that need to be staged into the workflow's scratch space by Pegasus.\"\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"transient\"\n    format_hint:\n      container: \"unknown\"\n      datasets: []\n      compression: \"unknown\"\n      layout_hint: \"unknown\"\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"many, runtime-determined\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: \"runtime_determined\"\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"runtime-determined\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"unknown\"\n    producer_task: null\n    consumer_tasks:\n      - \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n    lifecycle:\n      creation_phase: null\n      last_consumer_phase: \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n      retention_window: \"from workflow start to task:pegasus_stage_in completion\"\n      access_frequency_class: \"once\"\n      consumer_count: 1\n  - data_id: \"data:staged_input_files\"\n    name: \"Staged Input Files (Conceptual)\"\n    description: \"A conceptual data object representing all input files after they have been successfully staged into the workflow's working directory by Pegasus. These files are then consumed by various processing tasks.\"\n    category: \"intermediate\"\n    persistence: \"workflow_scoped\"\n    format_hint:\n      container: \"unknown\"\n      datasets: []\n      compression: \"unknown\"\n      layout_hint: \"unknown\"\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"many, runtime-determined\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: \"runtime_determined\"\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"runtime-determined\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"unknown\"\n    producer_task: \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n    consumer_tasks: []\n    lifecycle:\n      creation_phase: \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n      last_consumer_phase: null\n      retention_window: \"from task:pegasus_stage_in completion to workflow end\"\n      access_frequency_class: \"repeatedly\"\n      consumer_count: null\n  - data_id: \"data:final_workflow_results\"\n    name: \"Final Workflow Results (Conceptual)\"\n    description: \"A conceptual data object representing all final output files of the workflow (e.g., `mutation_overlap_tar_gz`, `frequency_tar_gz`) that are collected and staged out to long-term storage.\"\n    category: \"output\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format_hint:\n      container: \"unknown\"\n      datasets: []\n      compression: \"unknown\"\n      layout_hint: \"unknown\"\n      typical_request_size_kb: null\n    cardinality: \"many, runtime-determined\"\n    cardinality_source:\n      type: \"runtime_determined\"\n      controlling_parameter: null\n      config_file: null\n      possible_values: \"runtime-determined\"\n    estimated_size_hint: \"unknown\"\n    producer_task: null\n    consumer_tasks:\n      - \"task:pegasus_stage_out\"\n    lifecycle:\n      creation_phase: null\n      last_consumer_phase: \"task:pegasus_stage_out\"\n      retention_window: \"from final task completion to task:pegasus_stage_out completion\"\n      access_frequency_class: \"once\"\n      consumer_count: 1\npc_edges:\n  - edge_id: \"pc:pegasus_stage_in->individuals:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n    consumer: \"task:individuals\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:chromosome_vcf_raw\"\n      - \"data:columns_file\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"The single `pegasus_stage_in` task stages all input files, including multiple `data:chromosome_vcf_raw` files and a global `data:columns_file`. Multiple `individuals` tasks (one per VCF chunk) will then consume `data:chromosome_vcf_raw` files, and all will consume `data:columns_file` from the staged area.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"Input VCF files and the columns configuration file are staged from their source to the workflow's scratch space. Each `individuals` task instance reads its assigned VCF chunk and the common columns file from this staged location.\"\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: \"The `individuals` tasks cannot begin processing until their respective `data:chromosome_vcf_raw` and `data:columns_file` are fully staged and available.\"\n    communication_pattern: \"file_per_producer\"\n    data_volume_class: \"large\"\n  - edge_id: \"pc:pegasus_stage_in->sifting:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n    consumer: \"task:sifting\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:vep_annotation_vcf\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"The single `pegasus_stage_in` task makes multiple `data:vep_annotation_vcf` files available. Multiple `sifting` tasks (one per chromosome VEP file) will then consume these from the staged area.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"VEP annotation VCF files are staged from their source to the workflow's scratch space. Each `sifting` task instance reads its assigned VEP file from this staged location.\"\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: \"The `sifting` tasks cannot begin processing until their respective `data:vep_annotation_vcf` files are fully staged and available.\"\n    communication_pattern: \"file_per_producer\"\n    data_volume_class: \"large\"\n  - edge_id: \"pc:pegasus_stage_in->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n    consumer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n      - \"data:columns_file\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"The single `pegasus_stage_in` task makes multiple `data:population_file` instances and the `data:columns_file` available. Multiple `mutation_overlap` tasks (one per chromosome and population) will consume these from the staged area.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"Population data files and the columns configuration file are staged. Each `mutation_overlap` task reads its relevant `data:population_file` and the common `data:columns_file` from the staged location.\"\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: \"The `mutation_overlap` tasks cannot begin until their input population and columns files are staged.\"\n    communication_pattern: \"file_per_producer\"\n    data_volume_class: \"small\"\n  - edge_id: \"pc:pegasus_stage_in->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n    consumer: \"task:frequency\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n      - \"data:columns_file\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"Similar to `mutation_overlap`, the single `pegasus_stage_in` task makes multiple `data:population_file` instances and the `data:columns_file` available for consumption by multiple `frequency` tasks from the staged area.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"Population data files and the columns configuration file are staged. Each `frequency` task reads its relevant `data:population_file` and the common `data:columns_file` from the staged location.\"\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: \"The `frequency` tasks cannot begin until their input population and columns files are staged.\"\n    communication_pattern: \"file_per_producer\"\n    data_volume_class: \"small\"\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals\"\n    consumer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:individuals_chunk_tar_gz\"\n    pc_pattern: \"n_to_1\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"Multiple `individuals` tasks (processing chromosome chunks) produce intermediate data that is gathered and merged by a single `individuals_merge` task for each chromosome. This edge is conditional: if `--decaf` or `--pmc` are *not* set, each `individuals` task writes `data:individuals_chunk_tar_gz` files to disk, which `individuals_merge` then reads. If `--decaf` or `--pmc` *are* set, `individuals_mpi.py` (producer) transmits parsed data in-memory via MPI to `individuals_merge_mpi.py` (consumer). In this MPI path, `data:individuals_chunk_tar_gz` is not explicitly written by `individuals_mpi.py` but the corresponding data is reconstructed by `individuals_merge_mpi.py` into temporary files before producing `data:merged_individuals_tar_gz`.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"The data flow for this edge is conditional. In file-based execution, `individuals` tasks write tar.gz chunks to disk, which `individuals_merge` reads. In MPI-based execution, `individuals` tasks transmit parsed data directly to `individuals_merge` processes via MPI.\"\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: \"The `individuals_merge` task for a chromosome cannot begin until all `individuals` tasks for that chromosome have completed and made their data (files or in-memory streams) available.\"\n    communication_pattern: \"conditional: file_per_producer (if file-based execution) or in_memory (if MPI-based execution with Decaf/PMC)\"\n    data_volume_class: \"medium\"\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    consumer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:merged_individuals_tar_gz\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"A single `individuals_merge` task produces one `data:merged_individuals_tar_gz` file per chromosome. This file is then consumed by multiple `mutation_overlap` tasks, one for each population being analyzed for that chromosome.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"`mutation_overlap` tasks read the `data:merged_individuals_tar_gz` file for their respective chromosome.\"\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: \"The `mutation_overlap` tasks cannot begin for a given chromosome until its `data:merged_individuals_tar_gz` file is fully available.\"\n    communication_pattern: \"file_per_producer\"\n    data_volume_class: \"medium\"\n  - edge_id: \"pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    consumer: \"task:frequency\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:merged_individuals_tar_gz\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"A single `individuals_merge` task produces one `data:merged_individuals_tar_gz` file per chromosome. This file is then consumed by multiple `frequency` tasks, one for each population being analyzed for that chromosome.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"`frequency` tasks read the `data:merged_individuals_tar_gz` file for their respective chromosome.\"\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: \"The `frequency` tasks cannot begin for a given chromosome until its `data:merged_individuals_tar_gz` file is fully available.\"\n    communication_pattern: \"file_per_producer\"\n    data_volume_class: \"medium\"\n  - edge_id: \"pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:sifting\"\n    consumer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:sifted_snp_scores_txt\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"A single `sifting` task produces one `data:sifted_snp_scores_txt` file per chromosome. This file is then consumed by multiple `mutation_overlap` tasks, one for each population being analyzed for that chromosome.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"`mutation_overlap` tasks read the `data:sifted_snp_scores_txt` file for their respective chromosome.\"\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: \"The `mutation_overlap` tasks cannot begin for a given chromosome until its `data:sifted_snp_scores_txt` file is fully available.\"\n    communication_pattern: \"file_per_producer\"\n    data_volume_class: \"medium\"\n  - edge_id: \"pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    producer: \"task:sifting\"\n    consumer: \"task:frequency\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:sifted_snp_scores_txt\"\n    pc_pattern: \"1_to_n\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"A single `sifting` task produces one `data:sifted_snp_scores_txt` file per chromosome. This file is then consumed by multiple `frequency` tasks, one for each population being analyzed for that chromosome.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"`frequency` tasks read the `data:sifted_snp_scores_txt` file for their respective chromosome.\"\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: \"The `frequency` tasks cannot begin for a given chromosome until its `data:sifted_snp_scores_txt` file is fully available.\"\n    communication_pattern: \"file_per_producer\"\n    data_volume_class: \"medium\"\n  - edge_id: \"pc:mutation_overlap->pegasus_stage_out:n_to_1\"\n    producer: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    consumer: \"task:pegasus_stage_out\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:mutation_overlap_tar_gz\"\n    pc_pattern: \"n_to_1\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"Multiple `mutation_overlap` tasks (one per chromosome and population) produce final result files that are collected and staged out by the `pegasus_stage_out` task.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"The `pegasus_stage_out` task transfers all `data:mutation_overlap_tar_gz` files from the workflow's scratch space to their final destination.\"\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: \"The `pegasus_stage_out` task cannot complete for a given `data:mutation_overlap_tar_gz` file until that file has been fully produced by its respective `mutation_overlap` task.\"\n    communication_pattern: \"file_per_producer\"\n    data_volume_class: \"large\"\n  - edge_id: \"pc:frequency->pegasus_stage_out:n_to_1\"\n    producer: \"task:frequency\"\n    consumer: \"task:pegasus_stage_out\"\n    data_objects:\n      - \"data:frequency_tar_gz\"\n    pc_pattern: \"n_to_1\"\n    pc_pattern_rationale: \"Multiple `frequency` tasks (one per chromosome and population) produce final result files that are collected and staged out by the `pegasus_stage_out` task.\"\n    data_flow_description: \"The `pegasus_stage_out` task transfers all `data:frequency_tar_gz` files from the workflow's scratch space to their final destination.\"\n    coupling: \"tight\"\n    coupling_rationale: \"The `pegasus_stage_out` task cannot complete for a given `data:frequency_tar_gz` file until that file has been fully produced by its respective `frequency` task.\"\n    communication_pattern: \"file_per_producer\"\n    data_volume_class: \"large\"\nworkflow_graph:\n  integrity_hash: \"unknown_due_to_no_shell_access\"\n  last_generated: \"2026-03-04T00:00:00Z\"\n  dag_edges:\n    - from: \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n      to: \"task:individuals\"\n      via: \"pc:pegasus_stage_in->individuals:1_to_n\"\n    - from: \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n      to: \"task:sifting\"\n      via: \"pc:pegasus_stage_in->sifting:1_to_n\"\n    - from: \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n      to: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      via: \"pc:pegasus_stage_in->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    - from: \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n      to: \"task:frequency\"\n      via: \"pc:pegasus_stage_in->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    - from: \"task:individuals\"\n      to: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      via: \"pc:individuals->individuals_merge:n_to_1\"\n    - from: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      to: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      via: \"pc:individuals_merge->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    - from: \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      to: \"task:frequency\"\n      via: \"pc:individuals_merge->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    - from: \"task:sifting\"\n      to: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      via: \"pc:sifting->mutation_overlap:1_to_n\"\n    - from: \"task:sifting\"\n      to: \"task:frequency\"\n      via: \"pc:sifting->frequency:1_to_n\"\n    - from: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      to: \"task:pegasus_stage_out\"\n      via: \"pc:mutation_overlap->pegasus_stage_out:n_to_1\"\n    - from: \"task:frequency\"\n      to: \"task:pegasus_stage_out\"\n      via: \"pc:frequency->pegasus_stage_out:n_to_1\"\n  loop_groups: []\n  critical_path_hint: \"indeterminate from static analysis\"\n  control_flow:\n    has_iteration: true\n    iteration_description: \"The workflow iterates over each chromosome defined in `data.csv`, processing each one independently through chunking, merging, and sifting stages. The final analysis stages (mutation overlap and frequency) also iterate over combinations of chromosomes and populations.\"\n    has_conditional_branches: true\n    conditional_description: \"Conditional execution paths exist within the `individuals`, `individuals_merge`, and `sifting` tasks, primarily driven by `--bash-jobs`, `--decaf`, or `--pmc` flags, which determine whether bash scripts, Python scripts, or MPI-enabled Python scripts are used, affecting I/O access patterns and communication mechanisms.\"\n  stage_execution_order:\n    - \"stage:data_chunking\"\n    - \"stage:chromosome_processing\"\n    - \"stage:population_analysis\"\n  cross_reference:\n    task_to_stage:\n      \"task:pegasus_stage_in\": \"stage:data_chunking\"\n      \"task:individuals\": \"stage:data_chunking\"\n      \"task:individuals_merge\": \"stage:chromosome_processing\"\n      \"task:sifting\": \"stage:chromosome_processing\"\n      \"task:mutation_overlap\": \"stage:population_analysis\"\n      \"task:frequency\": \"stage:population_analysis\"\n      \"task:pegasus_stage_out\": \"stage:population_analysis\"\n    data_to_producer:\n      \"data:data_config_csv\": null\n      \"data:columns_file\": null\n      \"data:population_file\": null\n      \"data:chromosome_vcf_raw\": null\n      \"data:vep_annotation_vcf\": null\n      \"data:individuals_chunk_tar_gz\": \"task:individuals\"\n      \"data:merged_individuals_tar_gz\": \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      \"data:sifted_snp_scores_txt\": \"task:sifting\"\n      \"data:mutation_overlap_tar_gz\": \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      \"data:frequency_tar_gz\": \"task:frequency\"\n      \"data:raw_input_files\": null\n      \"data:staged_input_files\": \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n      \"data:final_workflow_results\": null\n    data_to_consumers:\n      \"data:data_config_csv\": []\n      \"data:columns_file\":\n        - \"task:individuals\"\n        - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n        - \"task:frequency\"\n      \"data:population_file\":\n        - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n        - \"task:frequency\"\n      \"data:chromosome_vcf_raw\":\n        - \"task:individuals\"\n      \"data:vep_annotation_vcf\":\n        - \"task:sifting\"\n      \"data:individuals_chunk_tar_gz\":\n        - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n      \"data:merged_individuals_tar_gz\":\n        - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n        - \"task:frequency\"\n      \"data:sifted_snp_scores_txt\":\n        - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n        - \"task:frequency\"\n      \"data:mutation_overlap_tar_gz\":\n        - \"task:pegasus_stage_out\"\n      \"data:frequency_tar_gz\":\n        - \"task:pegasus_stage_out\"\n      \"data:raw_input_files\":\n        - \"task:pegasus_stage_in\"\n      \"data:staged_input_files\": []\n      \"data:final_workflow_results\":\n        - \"task:pegasus_stage_out\"\nworkflow_patterns:\n  primary_pattern: \"hybrid\"\n  secondary_patterns:\n    - \"scatter_gather\"\n    - \"iterative\"\n    - \"conditional\"\n  classification_rationale: \"The workflow exhibits a hybrid pattern. It employs a scatter-gather approach for chromosome processing (multiple 'individuals' tasks scatter chunks, 'individuals_merge' gathers them). It is iterative as it processes each chromosome and then each population combination. Furthermore, it includes conditional execution paths for several tasks (e.g., 'individuals', 'individuals_merge', 'sifting') based on command-line flags, demonstrating a conditional pattern. The overall structure is not purely linear, pipeline, or broadcast, but a combination.\"\n  pattern_table_row: \"1000-genome | 3 | Many (dynamic) | 1_to_n, n_to_1 | File-based, In-memory (MPI)\"\nio_behavioral_hints:\n  - hint_id: \"hint:dynamic_io_access_pattern\"\n    description: \"The I/O access patterns for `task:individuals` and `task:individuals_merge` are dynamic and depend on runtime flags (`--bash-jobs`, `--decaf`, `--pmc`). This introduces variability in whether file-based (POSIX/Python serial) or in-memory (MPI) communication is used for intermediate data.\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    affected_data:\n      - \"data:individuals_chunk_tar_gz\"\n    potential_concern: \"unknown\"\n  - hint_id: \"hint:large_vcf_chunking\"\n    description: \"The `task:individuals` processes large VCF files by chunking them. If `ind_jobs` parameter leads to many small chunks, it could incur metadata overhead or many small file accesses.\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n    affected_data:\n      - \"data:chromosome_vcf_raw\"\n      - \"data:individuals_chunk_tar_gz\"\n    potential_concern: \"small_file_overhead\"\n  - hint_id: \"hint:in_memory_dataflow_potential\"\n    description: \"The MPI-based execution paths for `task:individuals` and `task:individuals_merge` (`--decaf` or `--pmc`) leverage in-memory data transfer for intermediate results, potentially reducing file I/O bottlenecks for these stages. However, `individuals_merge_mpi.py` still reconstructs temporary files before producing the final merged tarball.\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:individuals\"\n      - \"task:individuals_merge\"\n    affected_data:\n      - \"data:individuals_chunk_tar_gz\"\n    potential_concern: \"unknown\"\n  - hint_id: \"hint:multiple_consumers_per_input\"\n    description: \"Data objects like `data:merged_individuals_tar_gz` and `data:sifted_snp_scores_txt` are consumed by multiple downstream tasks (`task:mutation_overlap` and `task:frequency`). This implies potential for data reuse if caching or efficient sharing mechanisms are employed.\"\n    affected_tasks:\n      - \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n      - \"task:frequency\"\n    affected_data:\n      - \"data:merged_individuals_tar_gz\"\n      - \"data:sifted_snp_scores_txt\"\n    potential_concern: \"data_reuse\"\nexecution_profiles:\n  - profile_name: \"full_workflow\"\n    terminal_task_id: \"task:pegasus_stage_out\"\n    description: \"Represents the complete execution of the 1000 Genomes work